<Sequence DisplayName="Send Email via SendGrid" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_14">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>shared/SendEmail.xaml — SendGrid wrapper used by all three bots.</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<Sequence DisplayName="1. Guard" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_2">
<ui:Comment Text='TODO(Studio): If in_To is empty or not an email -&gt; out_ErrorCode = "INVALID_CONTACT", out_Retryable = False, exit' sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_1" />
</Sequence>
<Sequence DisplayName="2. Dry run" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_4">
<ui:Comment Text='TODO(Studio): If in_DryRun: log masked recipient, out_Success = True, out_MessageId = "DRYRUN-" &amp; Guid, exit' sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_3" />
</Sequence>
<TryCatch DisplayName="3. Call SendGrid" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="TryCatch_10">
<sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>Body:
  {"personalizations":[{"to":[{"email": in_To}]}],
   "from":{"email": in_FromEmail},
   "subject": in_Subject,
   "content":[{"type":"text/html","value": in_HtmlBody}]}

SendGrid returns 202 Accepted with an EMPTY body. The message id is in the
X-Message-Id response header, not the JSON — reading the body gets you nothing.

in_FromEmail must be a Single Sender verified in SendGrid, or every send
returns 403. That is a configuration fault, so treat 403 like 401: system
exception, stop the job.

  202                 success
  429, 5xx, timeout   out_Retryable = True
  400                 out_Retryable = False, INVALID_CONTACT
  401, 403            system exception — API key or sender not set up</sap2010:Annotation.AnnotationText>
<TryCatch.Try>
<Sequence DisplayName="HTTP Request" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Sequence_7">
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): POST https://api.sendgrid.com/v3/mail/send ; header Authorization: Bearer {in_ApiKey} ; JSON body below" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_5" />
<ui:Comment Text="TODO(Studio): 202 -&gt; out_Success = True, out_MessageId = X-Message-Id response header" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Comment_6" />
</Sequence>
</TryCatch.Try>
<TryCatch.Catches>
<Catch x:TypeArguments="s:Exception" sap2010:WorkflowViewState.IdRef="Catch_11">
<ActivityAction x:TypeArguments="s:Exception">
